# `power::zbase`

Impedance base of a per-unit system.

## Signature

```cpp
double power::zbase(const power::Base& base);
```

## What It Does

Returns `voltage^2 / power`, the impedance in ohms that equals `1` per unit.

## Parameters

`base`
: The power and voltage bases.

## Returns

The impedance base in ohms.

## Errors

Throws `std::invalid_argument` for a base that is not positive and finite.

## Interpretation and Use

Divide an impedance in ohms by it to get per unit.

